  "working_tree": "Uncommitted code-intelligence work; this receipt and documentation follow the frozen checks.",
  "shared_implementation": "The existing shared resource interpreter chooses original/created provenance and allowed script mutations. One descriptor-bound native revision/attribute reader supplies both native workers. Central original_revision validation serves eager capability admission and per-object checks. The constructor takes the actual root identity and plan separately, preserving physical binding while distinguishing file operations from editor-only changes.",
  "contract": [
    "Original native revisions now contain a bounded opaque attribute digest, in addition to descriptor identity/stat metadata. It covers sorted raw extended-attribute names and values, macOS descriptor ACLs or Linux ACL xattrs, and native semantic flags. The same descriptor is observed before and after reads; flag reads are also checked around collection. Only the digest is retained in analysis/journals.",
    "Each observation reserves working capacity before reading attributes. Limits are 64 KiB of names, 256 names, 1 MiB of names/values, 64 KiB of native ACL copy data and a shared 16 MiB working pool. Existing per-record, aggregate metadata, native response and snapshot limits remain unchanged. Unavailable access or bounded capacity produces a partial attribute observation rather than an empty-attribute assertion.",
    "New review-bearing plans with file operations require persistent original identities and complete attribute observations before authority claim. One original_revision helper also enforces that requirement at each actual original-resource match. The real captured root identity is still supplied separately from the plan.",
    "The shared interpreter continues to decide which original roots moved and which directory namespaces the application changed. Those expected time/namespace changes never exempt attribute digest, mode or ownership checks. Linux comparison retains unknown flag bits, excluding only the explicitly recorded internal storage-layout flags; macOS native flags are preserved in full.",
    "Real native fixtures reproduce four failures before the fix: both modes restored or cleaned an already-moved directory after an external xattr update while inode, mode, links, ownership, size and mtime stayed unchanged. Updated contracts use real original-LSP/HMAC verification, SQLite authority admission and paired HTTP/native execution, followed by service shutdown, grant expiry and provider invalidation.",
    "Both adapter contracts now run unchanged controls and xattr, ACL and nodump-flag changes for ambiguous transfer and irreversible cleanup. They preserve the complete private original tree and changed attributes, make no new LSP action query or command call, and do not republish an already-decided editor successor.",
    "Complete native resource capability is required only for plans declaring file operations. Text/command-only reviews retain their signed evidence without gaining a native resource capability. An actual macOS 257-attribute fixture previously rejected such a review; both authority profiles now validate its original HMAC, preserve ordinary reads and reject unexpected original-resource access with the partial witness.",
    "Fresh rebuilt installed Local and Remote resource/command/interruption workflows and declared-input rejection/acceptance pass with immutable durable LanguageReview and fresh initial manual authority. The same original metadata and new attribute contracts execute on macOS and Linux."
  ],
